Fields (readers, and SETF where writable):
  point  point2-d  Copied original coordinate.
  input-index  integer  Earliest matching original record index."))

(defclass datamunge:convex-hull-work (datamunge:native-object) ()
  (:documentation "Actual sorting, deduplication and two-scan work, with checked counters.
Comparison counts depend on the standard-library sort and original order.
For at least two distinct points each pass pushes each point once. Tests
count exact orientation requests; every nonpositive test causes one pop.
max_stack is the greatest length of either separate chain, not their sum.

**Example**

```cpp
const auto a=dm::geometry::convex_hull_analyze({{0,0},{1,0},{0,1}});
std::cout << a.work.distinct_points << ' ' << a.work.pushes; // 3 6
```

See also: ConvexHullAnalysis

Constructors:
  (make-convex-hull-work) → convex-hull-work

Fields (readers, and SETF where writable):
  input-points  integer  Fully validated original point count.
  distinct-points  integer  Unique coordinate count after sorting.
  sort-comparisons  integer  Actual lexicographic record comparisons.
  duplicate-comparisons  integer  Actual adjacent-equality comparisons.
  orientation-tests  integer  Exact determinant-sign calls during scans.
  pushes  integer  Actual separate-chain pushes.
  pops  integer  Actual non-left-turn removals.
  max-stack  integer  Maximum single-chain length reached."))

(defclass datamunge:hull-event (datamunge:native-object) ()
  (:documentation "Actual scan event, referring to indices in the trace's sorted unique points.
candidate is the pending point; point is the pushed/popped point, or candidate
for a test. a,b,turn are meaningful only for test events and otherwise zero.
stack_size is the actual size after the event (unchanged for tests). Together
these compact edits describe every stack state without quadratic snapshots.

**Example**

```cpp
const auto t=dm::geometry::convex_hull_trace({{0,0},{1,0}});
std::cout << t.events[0].stack_size; // 1
```

See also: ConvexHullTrace, HullPass, HullAction

Constructors:
  (make-hull-event) → hull-event

Fields (readers, and SETF where writable):
  pass  hull-pass  Producing scan direction.
  action  hull-action  Actual test, pop or push.
  candidate  integer  Pending sorted unique point.
  point  integer  Actual edited point, or candidate for a test.
  a  integer  Test's next-to-top point; otherwise zero placeholder.
  b  integer  Test's top point; otherwise zero placeholder.
  turn  integer  Exact test sign -1,0,+1; otherwise zero placeholder.
  stack-size  integer  Size immediately after this event."))

(defclass datamunge:convex-hull-analysis (datamunge:native-object) ()
  (:documentation "Owned strict hull, earliest original identities and actual work without history.
Vertices start at the lexicographic minimum and run counterclockwise, without
repeating the first. Collinear edge points are omitted. Empty gives no points;
one distinct point gives one; a collinear set gives its sorted two endpoints.
Identity vector aligns one-for-one with hull vertices.

**Example**

```cpp
const auto a=dm::geometry::convex_hull_analyze({{1,0},{0,0},{0,1}});
std::cout << a.hull.size() << ' ' << a.input_indices[0]; // 3 1
```

See also: convex_hull_analyze()

Constructors:
  (make-convex-hull-analysis) → convex-hull-analysis

Fields (readers, and SETF where writable):
  hull  (vector point2-d)  Owned unclosed strict hull.
  input-indices  (vector integer)  Earliest original identities in hull order.
  work  convex-hull-work  Actual producing operations."))

(defclass datamunge:convex-hull-trace (datamunge:native-object) ()
  (:documentation "Owned actual sorted identities, compact stack edits and completed scan chains.
lower/upper contain indices into sorted and include their endpoints. Inputs
with fewer than two distinct points take no scans and have empty chains/events.
Trace capture performs no extra sorting or orientation replay. All storage is
independent of the caller, result and other snapshots; O(n) extra space.

**Example**

```cpp
const auto t=dm::geometry::convex_hull_trace({{0,0},{1,0}});
std::cout << t.lower.size() << ' ' << t.upper.size(); // 2 2
```

See also: convex_hull_trace()

Constructors:
  (make-convex-hull-trace) → convex-hull-trace

Fields (readers, and SETF where writable):
  analysis  convex-hull-analysis  Actual hull, identities and work.
  sorted  (vector hull-indexed-point)  Actual sorted distinct input records.
  events  (vector hull-event)  Actual test/pop/push edits.
  lower  (vector integer)  Actual final lower stack.
  upper  (vector integer)  Actual final upper stack."))

