  distance  double-float  Finite nonnegative summed absolute loss for a computed result.
  path-a  (vector integer)  Owned zero-based a indices, from zero to a.size()-1.
  path-b  (vector integer)  Owned parallel b indices, from zero to b.size()-1."))

(defclass datamunge:dtw-work (datamunge:native-object) ()
  (:documentation "Logical work of the shared DTW recurrence and actual traceback.
These are counts, not time. Validation, allocation, copies, comparisons and
rendering are excluded. Each positive cell reads three predecessor slots,
including infinite boundary slots. Every returned pair counts one traceback step.

**Example**

```cpp
const auto r=dm::geometry::dynamic_time_warping_work({2},{5});
std::print(\"{} {} {}\\n\",r.work.cells,r.work.predecessor_reads,r.work.traceback_steps); // 1 3 1
```

See also: DTWComputation

Constructors:
  (make-dtw-work) → dtw-work

Fields (readers, and SETF where writable):
  cells  integer  Exactly a.size()*b.size() recurrence evaluations.
  predecessor-reads  integer  Three slots per recurrence cell, including borders.
  traceback-steps  integer  Number of actual output index pairs, including origin."))

(defclass datamunge:dtw-computation (datamunge:native-object) ()
  (:documentation "Owned ordinary result and logical work, without retained cost-table history.
Scratch consists of two cost rows and one predecessor byte per positive cell.
No input references survive return. Copies own independent result paths.

**Example**

```cpp
const auto c=dm::geometry::dynamic_time_warping_work({0,1},{0,1});
std::print(\"{} {}\\n\",c.result.distance,c.work.cells); // 0 4
```

See also: dynamic_time_warping_work(), DTWTrace

Constructors:
  (make-dtw-computation) → dtw-computation

Fields (readers, and SETF where writable):
  result  dtw-result  Optimal path and its unnormalized absolute loss.
  work  dtw-work  Actual recurrence and traceback counts."))

(defclass datamunge:dtw-trace (datamunge:native-object) ()
  (:documentation "Owned input, actual accumulated costs and chosen predecessors from one DTW run.
Positive cells are row-major at i*b.size()+j; sentinel border is implicit.
Costs and predecessor codes are captured during the original recurrence,
not reconstructed afterward. Infinite cells mark unrepresentable costs.
Logical capture entries are a.size()+b.size()+2*a.size()*b.size(): one
per input scalar, cost and direction. Result paths, rolling scratch rows,
scalar metadata and allocator bytes are excluded. Copies are independent.

**Example**

```cpp
const auto t=dm::geometry::dynamic_time_warping_trace({1},{4});
std::print(\"{} {}\\n\",t.cumulative[0],t.captured_entries); // 3 4
```

See also: dynamic_time_warping_trace(), dtw_trace_entries()

Constructors:
  (make-dtw-trace) → dtw-trace

Fields (readers, and SETF where writable):
  a  (vector double-float)  Owned first input, unchanged by alignment.
  b  (vector double-float)  Owned second input.
  cumulative  (vector double-float)  Actual positive-cell prefix costs, row-major.
  predecessors  (vector dtw-predecessor)  Actual selected directions, parallel to cumulative.
  result  dtw-result  Finite optimal distance and selected actual traceback.
  work  dtw-work  Counts from the same recurrence/traceback.
  captured-entries  integer  Complete logical capture cost described above."))

