Fields (readers, and SETF where writable):
  population-size  integer  Number of nests (candidate solutions) in the population.
  discovery-rate  double-float  pa: fraction of the worst nests discovered/abandoned each iteration. Yang & Deb's original paper headlines 0.25, but this implementation's \"replace a randomly chosen comparison nest\" Levy-flight rule (faithful to the paper) homogenizes the population fast enough at pa=0.25 that convergence quality becomes sharply seed-dependent on smooth objectives (verified: only 6/30 seeds converged well at pa=0.25, population_size=25 on a simple 3D sphere). 0.4 -- still within the commonly-used literature range -- injects enough fresh diversity each iteration to fix this at the default population size (verified: 30/30 seeds).
