(defclass datamunge:arima-options (datamunge:native-object) ()
  (:documentation "Model orders and optimizer settings for an ARIMA fit.

The regular orders are (p, d, q) and the seasonal orders are (P, D, Q) with period s.
Leave every seasonal field at zero for a plain ARIMA(p, d, q) model.

Constructors:
  (make-arima-options) → arima-options

Fields (readers, and SETF where writable):
  p  integer  Non-seasonal AR order (p).
  d  integer  Non-seasonal differencing order (d).
  q  integer  Non-seasonal MA order (q).
  seasonal-p  integer  Seasonal AR order (P).
  seasonal-d  integer  Seasonal differencing order (D).
  seasonal-q  integer  Seasonal MA order (Q).
  seasonal-period  integer  Seasonal period (s); must be nonzero when P, D, or Q is nonzero.
  include-mean  boolean  Fit an intercept (mean of the fully-differenced series). Only meaningful when d == 0 && seasonal_d == 0 -- matching R's arima(), a mean term is not fit on a series that has already been differenced to stationarity.
  de-population-size  integer  Population size of the differential-evolution optimizer.
  de-max-generations  integer  Maximum number of differential-evolution generations.
  coefficient-bound  double-float  Box constraint [-bound, bound] applied to every AR/MA coefficient during optimization.
  seed  integer  Random seed for the differential-evolution optimizer."))

(defclass datamunge:arima (datamunge:native-object) ()
  (:documentation "A Box-Jenkins seasonal ARIMA(p, d, q)(P, D, Q)_s model, fit to a single numeric
series by conditional sum of squares (CSS): the series is differenced (regular
d times, then seasonal D times with period s) to stationarity, the combined
AR/MA polynomials (regular composed with seasonal, via polynomial multiplication)
are estimated by minimizing the conditional residual sum of squares with
DifferentialEvolution, and forecasts are produced by recursing the fitted
difference equation forward and re-integrating through the differencing steps.

Setting seasonal_period == 0 (the default) reduces this to a plain, non-seasonal
ARIMA(p, d, q) model -- i.e. SARIMA is the general case, ARIMA the special case,
exactly as in R's arima()/statsmodels' SARIMAX().

Note: CSS estimation approximates the exact Gaussian likelihood by conditioning
on the first max(p + P*s, q + Q*s) observations rather than filtering the full
series (e.g. via a Kalman filter); it is a standard, textbook ARIMA fitting
method (R's arima(method = \"CSS\")) but will differ slightly from exact-ML fits.

Constructors:
  (make-arima y &optional (options (make-arima-options))) → arima"))

