(register-constructor 'datamunge:dual 2877 nil)
(defun datamunge:make-dual (value* &optional (derivative nil derivative-p))
  "A dual number value + derivative·ε (ε² = 0).

Seed the variable you differentiate with derivative 1 and constants with 0; every
operation then carries the exact derivative with respect to that seed.

**Example**

```cpp
const dm::Dual x(2.0, 1.0);  // seed d/dx
std::print(\"{}\\n\", x.multiply(x).derivative());  // 4
```

  (make-dual value* &optional (derivative 0d0)) → dual
    value*  double-float  Real part, the function value.
    derivative  double-float  Dual part, the derivative with respect to the seed (default 0)."
  (make-instance 'datamunge:dual :args (cond (derivative-p (list value* derivative)) (t (list value*)))))

(register-constructor 'datamunge:hyper-dual 2899 nil)
(defun datamunge:make-hyper-dual (value* &optional (eps1 nil eps1-p) (eps2 nil eps2-p) (eps1eps2 nil eps1eps2-p))
  "A hyper-dual number value + eps1·ε₁ + eps2·ε₂ + eps1eps2·ε₁ε₂ (ε₁² = ε₂² = 0).

Seed input i with eps1 = 1 and input j with eps2 = 1 (both on the same input for a
diagonal entry); the result's eps1eps2() is then the exact ∂²f/∂xᵢ∂xⱼ.

**Example**

```cpp
const dm::HyperDual x(3.0, 1.0, 1.0);
std::print(\"{}\\n\", x.multiply(x).eps1eps2());  // d²(x²)/dx² = 2
```

  (make-hyper-dual value* &optional (eps1 0d0) (eps2 0d0) (eps1eps2 0d0)) → hyper-dual
    value*  double-float  Real part, the function value.
    eps1  double-float  First derivative along the first seed direction (default 0).
