(defun datamunge:fem1-d-solve (mesh p q f left right)
  "Solve the steady P1 system for -(p*u')'+q*u=f with endpoint boundary data.
Follows FEM1D's mesh/coefficient/finite-arithmetic/nonsingular-pivot preconditions.
Uses three-point Gauss-Legendre quadrature of f times each local basis, natural
boundary terms and symmetric Dirichlet elimination, then Thomas elimination.
O(N) work/storage for N nodes; invokes the source three times per element.
No callback pointer is retained. Independent calls share no mutable state.

**Example**

```cpp
struct Unit final:dm::fem::ScalarField1D{double evaluate(double) override{return 1;}} source;
const auto r=dm::fem::FEM1D::solve(dm::fem::make_uniform_mesh1d(0,1,2),{1},{0},source,{},{});
std::print(\"{}\\n\",r.value_at(1)); // 0.125
```

**References**

- https://mfem.org/fem_weak_form/ ; native interval P1 and quadrature choices as FEM1D.

Errors (signalled as datamunge:native-error):
  std::invalid_argument: If p/q are empty or have the wrong lengths.
  std::bad_alloc: If assembly/result storage cannot be allocated; callback exceptions propagate.

See also: solve_builtin(), solve_transient()

  (fem1-d-solve mesh p q f left right) → fem1-d-result
    mesh  mesh1-d  Borrowed mesh with at least two finite strictly increasing nodes.
    p  (vector double-float)  Borrowed diffusion coefficient: length1 or one per element.
    q  (vector double-float)  Borrowed reaction coefficient: length1 or one per element.
    f  scalar-field1-d  Borrowed spatial source; evaluate() may have caller-owned side effects.
    left  boundary-condition1-d  Left endpoint condition, with outward normal -1.
    right  boundary-condition1-d  Right endpoint condition, with outward normal +1.
    → Owned original nodes and computed nodal values.

(Static method of fem1-d.)"
  (call 645 (list mesh p q f left right)))

(defun datamunge:fem1-d-solve-builtin (mesh p q source source-params left right)
  "Solve the steady system using an owned named spatial source, without a director callback.
Shares the live-source solver and its mathematical/precondition/storage contracts.
Sources: zero=0 (params unused); constant=c ({1}); linear=m*x+c ({1,0});
polynomial=sum(params[i]*x^i) (empty gives0); sine=A*sin(w*x+phase) ({1,1,0}).
Missing trailing parameters use those defaults; extra parameters are ignored
except polynomial, which uses all entries. Name matching is exact/case-sensitive.

**Example**

```cpp
const auto r=dm::fem::FEM1D::solve_builtin(dm::fem::make_uniform_mesh1d(0,1,2),{1},{0},\"constant\",{}, {},{});
std::print(\"{}\\n\",r.value_at(1)); // 0.125
```

**References**

- https://mfem.org/fem_weak_form/ ; source definitions are native convenience choices.

Errors (signalled as datamunge:native-error):
  std::invalid_argument: For an unknown source or malformed p/q lengths.
  std::bad_alloc: If owned parameter/assembly/result storage cannot be allocated.

See also: solve(), solve_transient_builtin()

  (fem1-d-solve-builtin mesh p q source source-params left right) → fem1-d-result
    mesh  mesh1-d  Borrowed valid finite interval mesh; unchanged.
    p  (vector double-float)  Borrowed scalar/per-element diffusion coefficient.
    q  (vector double-float)  Borrowed scalar/per-element reaction coefficient.
    source  string  Exact name zero, constant, linear, polynomial or sine.
    source-params  (vector double-float)  Borrowed positional source parameters, with defaults described above.
    left  boundary-condition1-d  Left endpoint data using outward normal -1.
    right  boundary-condition1-d  Right endpoint data using outward normal +1.
    → Owned computed nodal result, retaining no source or input reference.

(Static method of fem1-d.)"
  (call 646 (list mesh p q source source-params left right)))

(defun datamunge:fem1-d-solve-transient (mesh p q f left right u0 t-end dt)
  "Integrate u_t-(p*u')'+q*u=f with P1 space and actual backward-Euler time intervals.
Shares FEM1D's spatial/finite-arithmetic/nonzero-pivot preconditions. Source
and boundary data represent a time-independent model; the live callback is
actually reevaluated three times per element at every time advance, not cached.
Stores initial u0 as supplied, then imposes boundary data at later solves.
Nominal step dt is shortened at t_end; actual positive time differences enter
the mass term. Stops once t_end is reached, avoiding a duplicate rounded last
time even when ceil(t_end/dt) overestimates the number of advances.
O(S*N) work/output storage for S advances/N nodes, O(N) assembly temporaries;
no optional trace or quota. Backward Euler is unconditionally stable for the
coercive semidiscrete model, not a guarantee of arbitrary-step accuracy or
finite arithmetic for arbitrary parameters. Input arrays remain unchanged;
callback exceptions/side effects/concurrent safety belong to caller.

**Example**

```cpp
struct Zero final:dm::fem::ScalarField1D{double evaluate(double) override{return 0;}} source;
const auto t=dm::fem::FEM1D::solve_transient(dm::fem::make_uniform_mesh1d(0,1,2),{1},{0},source,{},{},{0,1,0},.5,.5);
std::print(\"{} {:.6f}\\n\",t.num_steps(),t.value_at(1,1)); // 2 0.142857
```

**References**

- Arnold (2012), Numerical Analysis of Partial Differential Equations, chapter5 section2.
  https://www-users.cse.umn.edu/~arnold/8445.f12/notes.pdf . Native load quadrature,
  fixed data and rounded/shortened time grid are implementation choices.

Errors (signalled as datamunge:native-error):
  std::invalid_argument: For fewer than two nodes, wrong coefficient/u0 lengths or nonpositive/nonfinite time controls.
  std::length_error: If frame counts, vector capacities or total scalar count cannot be represented.
  std::overflow_error: If rounded time products cannot advance before t_end.
  std::bad_alloc: If output/assembly storage cannot be allocated; callback exceptions propagate.

See also: solve_transient_builtin(), FEM1DTimeSeries

  (fem1-d-solve-transient mesh p q f left right u0 t-end dt) → fem1-d-time-series
    mesh  mesh1-d  Borrowed valid mesh with at least two finite increasing nodes.
    p  (vector double-float)  Borrowed scalar/per-element diffusion coefficient.
    q  (vector double-float)  Borrowed scalar/per-element reaction coefficient.
    f  scalar-field1-d  Borrowed spatial callback, reevaluated at every advance.
    left  boundary-condition1-d  Fixed left condition, with outward normal -1.
    right  boundary-condition1-d  Fixed right condition, with outward normal +1.
    u0  (vector double-float)  Borrowed finite initial nodal values, exactly one per mesh node.
    t-end  double-float  Positive finite final time, in time units.
    dt  double-float  Positive finite nominal time step in the same units; may exceed t_end.
    → Owned nodes, initial state and strictly advancing slices ending at t_end.

(Static method of fem1-d.)"
  (call 647 (list mesh p q f left right u0 t-end dt)))

