(defun datamunge:leapfrog-gaussian-acceptance (step-size num-steps sd &optional (angles nil angles-p))
  "Exact expected Metropolis acceptance of one HMC proposal (fixed step size and
number of leapfrog steps, unit mass) on a one-dimensional

`N(m,s^2)` target, started
in equilibrium.

In scaled coordinates `x=((q-m)/s,\\,p)` each leapfrog step is the linear map
`M=\\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\\\-h/2&1\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}1&h\\\\0&1\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\\\-h/2&1\\end{pmatrix}`
with `h=\\varepsilon/s`, `\\det M=1` and `\\operatorname{tr}M=2-h^2`, so it is stable
exactly when `\\varepsilon<2s`. Writing `x_0=r(\\cos\\phi,\\sin\\phi)` the energy error is
`\\Delta H=r^2f(\\phi)` with `f=\\tfrac12(|M^L(\\cos\\phi,\\sin\\phi)|^2-1)`, and because
`r^2/2\\sim\\text{Exp}(1)` the radial average of `\\min(1,e^{-\\Delta H})` is
`1/(1+2f)` for `f>0` and 1 otherwise. The angle is integrated numerically.

`\\varepsilon>0`.

`L\\geq1`.

`s>0`.

Errors (signalled as datamunge:native-error):
  std::invalid_argument: for non-positive arguments.

  (leapfrog-gaussian-acceptance step-size num-steps sd &optional (angles 4096)) → double-float
    step-size  double-float  Leapfrog step size
    num-steps  integer  Number of leapfrog steps
    sd  double-float  Target standard deviation
    angles  integer  Number of quadrature angles (at least 8).
    → The expected acceptance probability."
  (call 58 (cond (angles-p (list step-size num-steps sd angles)) (t (list step-size num-steps sd)))))

